      "notes": "Boltz, ColabFold and AlphaFold-style operators build MSAs locally with MMseqs2 against these databases, so no structure run needs the ColabFold API. Measurements on 2026-11-22: opendata.mmseqs.org served uniref30 at 2.9 MB/s and the environmental database at 9.4 MB/s from the compute host, while wwwuser.gwdg.de/~compbiol/colabfold/ dropped to 38 KB/s. The colabfold environment installs the mmseqs binary; set OPERON_COLABFOLD_MSA to point at a copy outside the resource root. The archive is not part of any environment's dependency gate: an environment stays ready without it, and only the operators that build MSAs locally need it (they report a clear error when it is absent)."
